# SIR — Semantic Intermediate Representation
# Authored by the SIGHTED decomposer. Language-neutral. Comments use '#' only.

UNIT isTypedArray
KIND FUNCTIONAL
ORACLE-CLASS deterministic
SIG isTypedArray(value: any) -> boolean
DEPENDS-ON none   # zero runtime deps; all helpers are inlined below

# ============================================================================
# EXPORT SHAPE
# ============================================================================
# CommonJS source: `module.exports = isTypedArray`.
# Emission target is a .mjs loaded via import(): the re-emitter MUST direct
#   export default isTypedArray
# i.e. the function itself is the module default export (importKind 'default').

# ============================================================================
# BEHAVIOR  (predicate: returns true iff `value` is a JS typed array)
# ============================================================================
# The real package selects ONE of two implementations at load time:
#
#   isTypedArray = nodeIsTypedArray ? baseUnary(nodeIsTypedArray) : baseIsTypedArray
#
# where nodeIsTypedArray = (the Node 'util' binding).isTypedArray IF it can be
# obtained via the legacy `process.binding('util')` call, else undefined.
#
# On the grading runtime (Node v24, VERIFIED) the Node fast path IS active, so
# the real package runs `nodeIsTypedArray(value)` — i.e. Node's internal
# util.types.isTypedArray, which inspects the [[TypedArrayName]] internal slot.
#
# BOTH paths are SPECIFIED to agree on the entire in-envelope input set (the
# value set genInputs can emit). A blind re-emitter MAY implement EITHER:
#   (A) the base path (tag-table predicate, fully specified below), OR
#   (B) the node path:  v => util.types.isTypedArray(v)   (Node 'util' import)
# Both produce identical results on every codec-faithful input in genInputs
# (VERIFIED by execution — 0 mismatches across the in-envelope battery; see
# PROVENANCE/verification note). Path (A) is the canonical, dependency-free
# reconstruction and is RECOMMENDED.
#
# ---- BASE PATH (canonical reconstruction) ----------------------------------
# baseIsTypedArray(value) returns the AND of three gates, short-circuiting:
#
#   NODE 1  isObjectLike(value)
#           := (!!value) && (typeof value === 'object')
#           # truthy AND typeof 'object'. null -> false (null is falsy AND
#           # typeof 'object', the !! short-circuits it out). undefined ->
#           # false. Numbers/strings/booleans/bigints/symbols/functions ->
#           # false (typeof not 'object', or function not 'object').
#           # NOTE: this is `!!value`, NOT `value != null`. They differ only
#           # for falsy-but-typeof-object values, of which JS has NONE
#           # (document.all is the lone host quirk; not in scope), so the two
#           # forms are observationally identical here. Use either.
#
#   NODE 2  isLength(value.length)
#           let n = value.length            # property read (NOT a throw site
#                                           # for any in-envelope value)
#           isLength(n) := (typeof n === 'number')
#                          && (n > -1)
#                          && (n % 1 === 0)         # integer-valued
#                          && (n <= MAX_SAFE_INTEGER)
#           MAX_SAFE_INTEGER = 9007199254740991     # 2^53 - 1, exact literal
#           # A real typed array's own `.length` is a non-negative integer in
#           # [0, MAX_SAFE_INTEGER] -> passes. A plain object lacking .length
#           # has value.length === undefined -> typeof 'number' fails -> false.
#           # An object {length: 3} passes this gate but fails NODE 3.
#
#   NODE 3  !!typedArrayTags[ Object.prototype.toString.call(value) ]
#           # baseGetTag in THIS bundle is EXACTLY:
#           #     objectToString.call(value)
#           #     where objectToString = Object.prototype.toString
#           # There is NO Symbol.toStringTag fast-path branch and NO
#           # null/undefined special-casing in this version (those were added
#           # in LATER lodash). It is a plain Object.prototype.toString.call.
#           # The result string is looked up in the typedArrayTags table; a
#           # missing key yields undefined -> !! -> false.
#
#   RESULT  NODE1 && NODE2 && NODE3   (all boolean; '&&' short-circuits)
#
# ---- typedArrayTags TABLE (complete, in-contract, NOT carried data) --------
# A plain object map from "[object X]" tag strings to boolean. Build it
# literally with these 24 entries (9 true, 15 false). Any tag NOT present
# (e.g. "[object Null]", "[object Undefined]", "[object Symbol]",
# "[object BigInt]", "[object Promise]", "[object GeneratorFunction]") is
# absent -> lookup undefined -> false.
#
#   MAPPED TRUE  (the 9 typed-array kinds):
#     "[object Float32Array]"      -> true
#     "[object Float64Array]"      -> true
#     "[object Int8Array]"         -> true
#     "[object Int16Array]"        -> true
#     "[object Int32Array]"        -> true
#     "[object Uint8Array]"        -> true
#     "[object Uint8ClampedArray]" -> true
#     "[object Uint16Array]"       -> true
#     "[object Uint32Array]"       -> true
#
#   MAPPED FALSE (15 explicit non-typed-array tags):
#     "[object Arguments]"   -> false
#     "[object Array]"       -> false
#     "[object ArrayBuffer]" -> false
#     "[object Boolean]"     -> false
#     "[object DataView]"    -> false
#     "[object Date]"        -> false
#     "[object Error]"       -> false
#     "[object Function]"    -> false
#     "[object Map]"         -> false
#     "[object Number]"      -> false
#     "[object Object]"      -> false
#     "[object RegExp]"      -> false
#     "[object Set]"         -> false
#     "[object String]"      -> false
#     "[object WeakMap]"     -> false
#
# (The explicit-false entries are behaviorally redundant with "absent key ->
#  false", but are listed so a reconstruction matches the source table shape.)
#
# NODE-PATH NOTE (Buffer): a Node Buffer is a Uint8Array subclass; both the
# node path and the base path return true for it (its toString tag is
# "[object Uint8Array]"). VERIFIED true for Buffer and Buffer.alloc(0).

# ============================================================================
# DETERMINISTIC TRUTH TABLE  (in-envelope — every value genInputs can emit)
# ============================================================================
# Each row computed by EXECUTING the real package at the source path; the
# codec round-trip (encode->JSON->decode) preserves the listed result.
#
#   Uint8Array  (any byte contents, incl. empty)  -> true
#   Buffer      (any byte contents, incl. empty)  -> true   # decodes to Buffer
#   Array       (incl. empty [])                  -> false
#   plain object {} / {a:1}                        -> false
#   object {length: <int>}  (no TA tag)            -> false  # passes NODE2, fails NODE3
#   Set                                            -> false
#   Map                                            -> false
#   RegExp                                         -> false
#   string                                         -> false  # typeof not 'object'
#   number (incl. integers, floats)                -> false
#   NaN, Infinity, -Infinity                       -> false
#   -0                                             -> false
#   bigint                                         -> false  # typeof 'bigint'
#   boolean (true/false)                           -> false
#   boxed Number / boxed String / boxed Boolean    -> false  # tag mapped false; no .length
#   null                                           -> false
#   undefined                                      -> false

# ============================================================================
# OUT-OF-ENVELOPE  (behavior specified here; EXCLUDED from genInputs because
#                   the oracle codec cannot carry the value faithfully — it
#                   would corrupt the stored arg and produce a false expected)
# ============================================================================
# These are NOT bugs in the unit — they are limits of the persistence codec.
# Their TRUE behavior under the REAL package (computed by execution) is:
#
#   Int8Array, Uint8ClampedArray, Int16Array, Uint16Array, Int32Array,
#   Uint32Array, Float32Array, Float64Array
#       REAL RESULT: true  (all 8 are typed arrays).
#       WHY EXCLUDED: the codec's u8 branch is `value instanceof Uint8Array`,
#       which is FALSE for these kinds. They fall through to the generic-object
#       branch and are stored as a plain {"0":..,"1":..} index map, which
#       decodes to a PLAIN OBJECT -> the unit would then return false. The
#       codec flips true->false. VERIFIED. Therefore they cannot be graded and
#       are kept out of genInputs. (Only Uint8Array & Buffer represent the
#       TRUE class in the gradable set.)
#
#   ArrayBuffer            REAL RESULT: false  (tag "[object ArrayBuffer]";
#                          also no integer .length). Codec stores it as a
#                          generic object; not emitted to avoid ambiguity.
#   DataView               REAL RESULT: false  (tag "[object DataView]";
#                          .byteLength not .length). Not codec-representable
#                          as itself; excluded.
#   function / arrow       REAL RESULT: false  (typeof 'function', not
#                          'object'). The codec DROPS function-valued data;
#                          not emitted.
#   Symbol                 REAL RESULT: false  (typeof 'symbol'). Not JSON/
#                          codec representable; excluded.
#
#   ADVERSARIAL DIVERGENCE (documented; NOT emittable and would diverge BETWEEN
#   the two impl paths — kept out so quorum is not poisoned):
#     - plain object with Symbol.toStringTag === 'Uint8Array' and a numeric
#       .length: BASE path -> true (toString yields the TA tag); NODE path
#       -> false (no internal slot). The real package on Node returns FALSE.
#       Not codec-carryable (Symbol key is dropped) -> excluded.
#     - typed array whose own `.length` has been redefined out of range, or
#       Object.create(Uint8Array.prototype): the two paths diverge and/or the
#       base path THROWS reading .length. Not codec-carryable -> excluded.
#   A re-emitter implementing the NODE path (util.types.isTypedArray) matches
#   the real package on ALL of these; one implementing the BASE path matches
#   on every in-envelope input but would differ on these adversarial values.
#   Since none are emittable, either reconstruction passes quorum.

# ============================================================================
# ERROR / THROW BEHAVIOR
# ============================================================================
# For EVERY in-envelope input (everything genInputs emits) the unit does NOT
# throw — it returns a boolean. The base path's `value.length` read is the
# only potential throw site, and it cannot throw for any in-envelope value
# (plain property read on objects, or short-circuited away by NODE1 for
# primitives/null/undefined). No throw vectors are in scope.

# ============================================================================
# PURITY / SEAM
# ============================================================================
# Pure. No clock, RNG, env, fs, or network read. No mutation of the argument
# or any global. The load-time selection of node-vs-base path is an ambient
# capability probe (process.binding('util')); it is NOT an input-dependent
# seam and both selected paths are specified to agree on all in-scope inputs,
# so the unit is ORACLE-CLASS deterministic (value mode). No seam injection,
# no quarantine, no side-effect harness (read-only predicate).

ORACLE value -> oracle.json

# ============================================================================
# SCOPE
# ============================================================================
# IN-CONTRACT LOGIC (reproduce exactly):
#   - the 3-gate base predicate (isObjectLike, isLength, tag-table lookup),
#   - the complete 24-entry typedArrayTags table (above),
#   - MAX_SAFE_INTEGER = 9007199254740991,
#   - baseGetTag == Object.prototype.toString.call (no toStringTag branch),
#   - the default-export shape.
# CARRIED DATA: none. (The 24-entry tag table is small in-contract logic,
#   transcribed in full above; it is NOT a carried-data table and there is no
#   <unit>.carried.json.)
# OUT-OF-CONTRACT: none (no stateful mutators / side APIs).
# OUT-OF-ENVELOPE (codec limits; specified above, excluded from genInputs):
#   the 8 non-Uint8Array typed-array kinds (real result true), ArrayBuffer,
#   DataView, functions, Symbols, and the adversarial divergence inputs.

